ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":147,"prev":149,"next":151,"titles":153,"firmware":46},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":20,"status":21,"firmware":22,"facts":27,"procedures":65,"parameters":88,"related":116,"body":122,"sources":123,"official_url":31,"controls":132},"mix.levels-pans-sends","Levels, pans and sends",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"track level","track volume","volume","pan","panning","fx send","send level","channel strip","mix",10,"knowledge/manual/units/mix/levels-pans-sends.md",{"modes":17,"screens":18},[13],[19],"M1","On mix `M1` the four encoders set the selected track's FX I send, FX II send, pan and level; clicking `E3` centres the pan and clicking `E4` mutes the track.","current",{"min":23,"changed_in":24,"guide_version":25,"verified_on":26},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[28,33,37,42,48,52,55,58,62],{"id":29,"text":30,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"page","`M1` in mix mode is the page for levels, pans and sends; a track key chooses which track the encoders adjust.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/mix#levels-pans-and-sends","official",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":36,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"midi","Over MIDI, CC7 sets a track's level and CC10 its pan, each on the track's own channel (1–16).","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/midi-references",{"id":38,"text":39,"source":40,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":41},"midi-sends","On an instrument track's channel, CC38 and CC39 set its FX I and FX II sends — presumably the same values this page shows.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#33-instrument-tracks-18-synth-drum-sampler-multisampler-engines","community",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":45,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":46,"confidence":47},"track-send-page","Instrument tracks repeat these sends on their `M3` shift layer, whose rows run aux out, tape, FX I, FX II from the top — FX I on `E3`, FX II on `E4`. TE's drawing of that page puts FX II above FX I; the device does not.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#23-filter-instrument-m3","1.1.33","verified",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":51,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":46,"confidence":47},"screen","The page draws eight columns, one per track, each with its number, a level line and a pan dot along the bottom; CC7 and CC10 sent over MIDI move them as they arrive.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#210-mixer",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":51,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":46,"confidence":47},"send-display","Turning `E1` or `E2` briefly swaps the selected track's column for two boxed labels, I and II, each with a dark bar rising to its send level; after about a second the column comes back.",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":51,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":46,"confidence":47},"cc38-quiet","Sending CC38 changes a track's FX I send without calling up that I and II display.",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":61,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":41},"held-keys","Holding several track keys on this page edits those tracks together. A turn of an encoder moves every held instrument track by the same amount, each clamped at its own limit. The strips left out lose their bars, which fall to the foot, and their numbers and dots, and the held strips show theirs (three videos, OS 1.0.x and 1.1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log",{"id":63,"text":64,"source":61,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":41},"muted-strip","A muted strip draws its bar in grey and its lines in a second grey. A video on OS 1.0.13 showed no lines at all on the lightest strip, a single sighting.",[66,78],{"id":67,"goal":68,"preconditions":69,"steps":70,"result":26,"source":31,"firmware_min":26,"verified_on":26,"confidence":32},"set-level","Set a track's level",[],[71,73,76],{"keys":72,"note":26,"set":26},"mix → M1",{"keys":74,"note":75,"set":26},"Tn","select the track",{"keys":77,"note":26,"set":26},"turn E4",{"id":79,"goal":80,"preconditions":81,"st